DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about fire in the Southern Blue Ridge Mou
 ntains? Join us on September 26th for the 3rd biannual Southern Blue Ridge
  Fire Fair\, a free event for landowners\, curious minds and prospective e
 mployees of fire and natural resources. We will hear from Adam Warwick\, S
 tewardship Manager for The Nature Conservancy\, on the role and importance
  of fire in our region. This will be followed by a networking event with l
 ocal natural resource professionals to learn more about job opportunities\
 , funding\, technical assistance and other available resources. A free lun
 ch will be provided\, followed by a tour of a burn unit on the Warren Wils
 on College Forest with Dr. Armin Weise\, Assistant Professor of Forest Man
 agement at Western Carolina University\, and Juniper Odell\, Prescribed Fi
 re Specialist with the Nature Conservancy. They will be leading a discussi
 on on the ecology of the site and how to properly conduct a controlled bur
 n. The event will be held in 110 Boon Hall and will begin at 9:00am. The e
 vent is free.
GEO:35.610089;-82.44138
LOCATION:Myron Boon Hall\, 110
SUMMARY:Southern Blue Ridge Fire Fair
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/southern-blue-ridge-fi
 re-fair-2489
END:VEVENT
