DESCRIPTION:This community-based therapeutic art project taps into the tran
 sformative power of altered books to tell our stories of Hurricane Helene 
 through the visual arts. Together\, we join with the many others who are s
 haping the narrative of our community’s collective experience of the sto
 rm and recovery. So far over 400 pages have been created as part of a mult
 i-volume project that has been displayed at the RAD Hotel in the River Art
 s District and other places in the region. Join us for this workshop\, whi
 ch is open to all and will be co-led by Warren Wilson students enrolled in
  the Art of Expressive Arts Therapy (SWK2250 & EAT2250). You'll learn how 
 to make an altered book and have an opportunity to create a page for the T
 urning the Page on Helene project!
GEO:35.610089;-82.44138
LOCATION:Myron Boon Hall\, 110
SUMMARY:Turning the Page on Helene: Story sharing through artistically alte
 red books!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/turning-the-page-on-he
 lene-story-sharing-through-artistically-altered-books
CATEGORIES:Social
CATEGORIES:Information Session & Training
END:VEVENT
