DESCRIPTION:Two years after Helene\, graduate students in Warren Wilson’s
  MS in Applied Climate Studies (MACS) program will present on the process 
 and outcomes of their engaged research projects. These projects sit at the
  center of the MACS program\, which prioritizes learning through both coop
 eration and application. From their first week\, MACS students are guided 
 in linking their classroom material with impactful projects. Students spen
 d two years working collaboratively with peers and alongside established c
 ommunity partners throughout their degree\, leaving the program with concr
 ete experience and skills in addressing present and pressing climate chang
 e challenges. Insights about building more resilient communities and ecosy
 stems will be shared.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Partnering for our future: WWC Applied Climate Studies
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/partnering-for-our-fut
 ure-warren-wilsons-applied-climate-studies-program-makes-recovery-and-resi
 lience-the-center-of-learning
END:VEVENT
