DESCRIPTION:Join Warren Wilson College for a Nielsen Big Idea Lecture featu
 ring Ladelle McWhorter\, Chair of Gender & Sexuality Studies at the Univer
 sity of Richmond.\n \n\nIn her talk\, “What Does Homophobia Have to Do W
 ith Racism? Let’s Look at the History\,” McWhorter will explore the hi
 storical connections between homophobia\, racism\, and systems of oppressi
 on. Drawing from her scholarship and decades of work in social justice\, s
 he will examine how these histories intersect and continue to shape our co
 mmunities today.\n \n\nMcWhorter is the author of Bodies and Pleasures\, R
 acism and Sexual Oppression in Anglo-America and Unbecoming Persons. She h
 as worked for social justice for more than thirty years with Virginia Orga
 nizing\, a grassroots organization dedicated to dismantling racism\, fight
 ing poverty and environmental injustice\, and training ordinary Virginians
  to advocate for themselves and their communities.
GEO:35.610912;-82.442142
LOCATION:Canon Lounge in Gladfelter Student Center
SUMMARY:Nielsen Big Idea Lecture: What Does Homophobia Have to Do With Raci
 sm?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.warren-wilson.edu/event/nielsen-big-idea-lectu
 re-what-does-homophobia-have-to-do-with-racism
CATEGORIES:Lecture
END:VEVENT
